{
  "chapter.0A36778321D0E80E.title": "10 • RFTools: Build, Process and Travel",
  "task.4E477056FB2A25BA.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.364B1F0F21B55ACF.title": "Start here: RFTools",
  "quest.364B1F0F21B55ACF.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.364B1F0F21B55ACF.quest_desc": [
    "RFTools is a family of practical machines. Builder shapes, places or removes blocks using cards; Utility adds crafting, displays and teleportation; Storage offers modular inventories and a scanner for existing chests. You can adopt one useful tool without building the entire family.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/rftools.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• Storage Tools",
    "• Builder & Cards",
    "• Workshop Utilities",
    "• Travel & Projects",
    "",
    "Your route: power and manuals -> storage modules/scanner -> controlled Builder job -> quarry distinctions -> crafters -> screens and transport -> a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.7A18FB30B819D5BB.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.05F4F827AAFA1FC8.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.05F4F827AAFA1FC8.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.05F4F827AAFA1FC8.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.004DD68AB46919DE.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.57DD9B9201AB5318.title": "Read the right manual",
  "quest.57DD9B9201AB5318.quest_subtitle": "Storage Tools",
  "quest.57DD9B9201AB5318.quest_desc": [
    "Builder, Utility and Storage are separate RFTools modules with different interfaces. Their installed manuals explain the exact controls available here.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Find the RFTools manuals in JEI and inspect one page from each installed module. Choose a small powered test area, with an energy buffer and ordinary input/output chests.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "RFTools Dimensions is a separate mod. These quests teach the installed Builder, Utility and Storage tools, not dimension creation."
  ],
  "task.0B222471AC249655.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.51D92DD2423142C2.title": "Storage with a removable module",
  "quest.51D92DD2423142C2.quest_subtitle": "Storage Tools",
  "quest.51D92DD2423142C2.quest_desc": [
    "Modular Storage holds items in a storage module. The module is important: it carries the contents and determines capacity.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Craft Modular Storage and a compatible storage module from JEI. Insert the module, add a few test items, and learn its sorting, filtering and crafting interface.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Treat a filled module as valuable storage. Check upgrade recipes and component handling before replacing or crafting with one."
  ],
  "task.1F033E11E3C7EC14.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.74591E725FAF9178.title": "Find items across existing chests",
  "quest.74591E725FAF9178.quest_subtitle": "Storage Tools",
  "quest.74591E725FAF9178.quest_desc": [
    "A Storage Scanner provides an interface to nearby inventories without requiring you to move everything into one new storage system.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Power the scanner, place two labeled test chests within range, set its radius and scan. Search for a known item and verify which inventory contains it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A scan discovers accessible inventories in its area. A chest outside the radius or unloaded area is not automatically part of the system."
  ],
  "task.0BC9376A4B7D3448.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5B613DE6E3221667.title": "Decide which inventories are routable",
  "quest.5B613DE6E3221667.quest_subtitle": "Storage Tools",
  "quest.5B613DE6E3221667.quest_desc": [
    "Scanner visibility and permission to use an inventory for routing are different concerns. You may want to see a supply chest without making it a general insertion destination.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the scanner's inventory list and routable settings. Enable only your test storage for automation, then verify insertion/extraction behavior with a small stack.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Avoid enabling every machine buffer and personal chest at once. Deliberate routing prevents an item from ending up in an unexpected inventory."
  ],
  "task.189C32C208FDD4BB.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4737630D28A02AC2.title": "Take storage access with you",
  "quest.4737630D28A02AC2.quest_subtitle": "Storage Tools",
  "quest.4737630D28A02AC2.quest_desc": [
    "A Storage Control Module links the supported tablet interface to a scanner for convenient remote access.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Find the Storage Control Module and tablet in JEI. Follow their tooltips/manual to link the module to your scanner, assemble the tablet setup and test retrieving one item nearby.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The scanner still needs power, accessible inventories and loaded chunks. The old Remote Storage system is different from scanner/tablet access."
  ],
  "task.23D17BCE00B25418.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3F952649493333D5.title": "The Builder follows a card",
  "quest.3F952649493333D5.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.3F952649493333D5.quest_desc": [
    "The Builder is a powered executor. Its inserted card defines the operation and area; supplying FE alone does not tell it what to do.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a Builder in an empty test area, supply modest power, and inspect its card slot, redstone control and preview/support controls. Start with an ordinary placement shape card from JEI.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "ATM10 replaces the Builder recipe with one requiring Allthemodium nuggets. Leave it disabled while configuring the area. Card names matter: placement, quarry, clearing, void and pump operations have different consequences."
  ],
  "task.262EBF9209F9E14F.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.636065F5A7FED2F4.title": "Select and preview a tiny area",
  "quest.636065F5A7FED2F4.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.636065F5A7FED2F4.quest_desc": [
    "Shape size, offset and anchor determine where the Builder acts. A wrong offset can put an otherwise correct shape in the wrong place.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Configure a small box in the card GUI, or follow the card's selection tooltip to select corners. Use the Builder's preview/support feature to inspect every edge before enabling it.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "FIRST CARD: Use a normal Shape Card for placement, choose a hollow box and small dimensions such as 5 by 5 by 5. Preview/support mode shows the selection relative to the Builder. The diagram is a workflow, not a multiblock blueprint.",
    "",
    "VERIFY OFFSET: Walk around all six boundaries and confirm the selected volume is clear of machines. Leave the Builder disabled until the preview matches your intended shell. This catches coordinate mistakes before they become a building or quarrying job.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Begin with a small hollow shape in open space. Zero offset centers a shape relative to the Builder; it does not necessarily mean the box starts at your feet.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/rftools.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.42313B9C694153EE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0C97D372DE4192E4.title": "Place a test structure",
  "quest.0C97D372DE4192E4.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.0C97D372DE4192E4.quest_desc": [
    "A placement job consumes building materials from an accessible supply and needs energy while working.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Provide an ordinary building block in the correct adjacent inventory, enable the Builder and complete your small previewed shape. Disable it and inspect the finished result.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If nothing happens, check redstone state, energy, the card operation and material access before increasing area size."
  ],
  "task.32C691B49E97DEA8.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3D12D37BED4FF5CA.title": "Quarry cards: understand the difference",
  "quest.3D12D37BED4FF5CA.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.3D12D37BED4FF5CA.quest_desc": [
    "A normal quarry removes blocks and replaces them with filler; a clearing quarry leaves the excavated area empty. Silk and fortune variants change harvesting behavior.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare the available quarry cards in JEI and the installed manual. Choose the behavior you actually want, then prepare a disposable small test area with a chest able to accept the drops.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Void operations remove blocks without keeping their drops. Do not substitute a void card for a quarry just because both clear an area."
  ],
  "task.2AB753B86F80B303.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5594BD3A263C42A6.title": "Run a controlled quarry test",
  "quest.5594BD3A263C42A6.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.5594BD3A263C42A6.quest_desc": [
    "A quarry is useful only when its bounds, output capacity and stop controls are predictable.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Preview a tiny quarry region away from structures, connect output storage, supply power and run one test. Confirm drops arrive, then stop and inspect the region before enlarging it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Claims, protected blocks, energy cost and full output can all stop progress. Keep the output visible and retain a way to disable the machine immediately."
  ],
  "task.6C18E631DCCC3F93.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2C7AAE8529DCE989.title": "Pump liquids separately",
  "quest.2C7AAE8529DCE989.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.2C7AAE8529DCE989.quest_desc": [
    "Pump cards handle liquids and need a destination that can store the extracted fluid. A clearing variant changes what remains behind.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the pump-card page, preview a small water area and connect a compatible tank. Run a short test and verify both the tank contents and the resulting world area.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Never assume an item chest can store pumped fluid. Confirm the tank accepts the exact fluid and has enough space."
  ],
  "task.219853E57B57DA49.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0AB1155414A36BE4.title": "Scan a structure for construction",
  "quest.0AB1155414A36BE4.quest_subtitle": "Builder & Cards",
  "quest.0AB1155414A36BE4.quest_desc": [
    "The Builder Scanner records shape information for the building tools. It is different from the Storage Scanner that searches inventories.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the Scanner page. Supply its input card with a small area definition, scan a disposable arrangement and inspect the output card. Compare the result before using it in a construction workflow.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start with a tiny pattern of cheap blocks. A successful scan does not supply the materials needed to reproduce the structure."
  ],
  "task.2D464B76CFF5DB13.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.47A9AE97A58A4A5C.title": "Craft repetitive recipes",
  "quest.47A9AE97A58A4A5C.quest_subtitle": "Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.47A9AE97A58A4A5C.quest_desc": [
    "An RFTools Crafter stores recipes and processes them from its internal inventory. Tier 3 supports multiple recipe steps in one machine.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Power a Crafter, teach one simple recipe and provide ingredients. Set the recipe's result handling deliberately, then verify the output before adding an intermediate recipe.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "TWO-STAGE RECIPE: Teach logs -> planks and planks -> sticks. Keep intermediate planks inside the Crafter for the second recipe; send the final sticks to the output. If both recipes send everything outward, the second one never receives its ingredient.",
    "",
    "REMEMBER SLOTS: Reserve ingredient slots before feeding a large amount of logs. Test with a small batch and inspect where each result goes. Throughput upgrades are useful only once recipe order and internal/external result handling are correct.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Output handling controls whether an intermediate stays available internally or leaves the machine. Wrong handling can starve a later recipe even with plenty of raw materials."
  ],
  "task.01CBDC1CAECE91DD.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7B7A21506AF0F888.title": "Remember ingredient slots",
  "quest.7B7A21506AF0F888.quest_subtitle": "Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.7B7A21506AF0F888.quest_desc": [
    "Remembered slots reserve inventory positions for specific ingredients. This prevents one abundant resource from occupying every available slot.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use the Crafter's Remember controls to reserve your ingredients, then supply them in uneven quantities. Verify the less common ingredient still has room when it arrives.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use Forget when changing recipes and inspect every old reservation. A stale slot assignment can look like a transport failure."
  ],
  "task.3E52BD893849BD26.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.68F12FB45632AD4E.title": "A screen for the workshop",
  "quest.68F12FB45632AD4E.quest_subtitle": "Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.68F12FB45632AD4E.quest_desc": [
    "Screens and modules display selected information. The Screen Controller supplies the powered support for screens in its working area.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Power a Screen Controller, place a nearby screen, add one suitable information module and scan/configure it according to the manual. Show one useful stock or machine reading.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start inside the controller's ordinary range. A blank screen may lack a configured module, a scanned controller connection or power."
  ],
  "task.4F2C83D60AA58E52.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7DF19F62049AD56C.title": "Build a teleport pair",
  "quest.7DF19F62049AD56C.quest_subtitle": "Travel & Projects",
  "quest.7DF19F62049AD56C.quest_desc": [
    "Matter Transmitters send you to Matter Receivers through a dialed connection. The Dialing Device establishes the route.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build powered transmitter and receiver endpoints with a safe arrival space. In the Dialing Device select the source, select the destination, then use Dial or Dial Once and test a short local trip.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "THREE DEVICES: The transmitter is the departure point, the receiver is the named arrival point, and the Dialing Device chooses the connection. Power the endpoints and dial a nearby receiver with clear headroom.",
    "",
    "ROUND TRIP: A destination receiver does not by itself send you home. Provide a reverse setup or bind a charged porter to your home receiver. Test both directions before relying on a remote destination.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a physical return route for the first test. Verify destination power, access and chunk availability before relying on a long-distance link."
  ],
  "task.4CDC68EED43843CF.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5799453D63DA415C.title": "Carry a route home",
  "quest.5799453D63DA415C.quest_subtitle": "Travel & Projects",
  "quest.5799453D63DA415C.quest_desc": [
    "A charged porter gives portable access to an assigned Matter Receiver. It still depends on a working destination.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Find the Charged Porter in JEI, charge it and bind it to your receiver using its tooltip instructions. Test from nearby, then compare the advanced version if you need multiple destinations.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check charge and binding before exploring. A portable return device is not a replacement for a powered, loaded and safe receiving area."
  ],
  "task.1BFB34ECBFB14A5B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7B9628162E1461FD.title": "Infusion and specialist machines",
  "quest.7B9628162E1461FD.quest_subtitle": "Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.7B9628162E1461FD.quest_desc": [
    "RFTools upgrades and specialist tools can improve a working setup, but their benefits depend on the particular machine.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the installed manual's infusion information and inspect improvements for one machine you already use. Browse the Environmental Controller and shield system as optional projects with their own module and power requirements.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Upgrade for a measured need. Larger areas, stronger effects or faster work can raise power demand and do not fix a misconfigured card or recipe."
  ],
  "task.089652F610B6361E.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.53AA0C3333600B35.title": "Troubleshoot the operation, not just power",
  "quest.53AA0C3333600B35.quest_subtitle": "Travel & Projects",
  "quest.53AA0C3333600B35.quest_desc": [
    "A powered RFTools machine can still have the wrong card, invalid area, blocked output, missing module or disabled control state.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the machine's status, operation/card, redstone mode, area or range, resource supply and output space. Reduce the job to a tiny known example and compare it with the manual.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Storage Scanner and Builder Scanner solve different problems. Check the exact block name when a tutorial seems to describe an interface you do not have."
  ],
  "task.645FA1C7A1EC9FA8.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5913F44ED94E1822.title": "Project: a practical workshop expansion",
  "quest.5913F44ED94E1822.quest_subtitle": "Travel & Projects",
  "quest.5913F44ED94E1822.quest_desc": [
    "RFTools is most useful as a collection of tools that solve your own building and logistics problems.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use a previewed Builder job for a small workshop shell, a Crafter for one recurring ingredient and a scanner or screen for supply access. Add a tested return receiver if useful, then document how each system stops and restarts.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep quarrying and destructive shape operations away from the workshop. Save the card settings for the construction job you have already verified."
  ],
  "task.3C32538A7B37AE7C.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.444912A5B494E81A.title": "The module holds the inventory",
  "quest.444912A5B494E81A.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Storage Tools",
  "quest.444912A5B494E81A.quest_desc": [
    "The removable storage module is the valuable part of Modular Storage once it contains items. The block and module serve different roles.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Put a few named test items in Modular Storage, inspect the module and learn how the interface reports capacity. Read the upgrade recipe before using a filled module as an ingredient.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start with disposable items. Never discover whether a recipe preserves contents by testing it on your only valuable storage module."
  ],
  "task.2065B133CF2095AE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2FDE8EE1489DEC78.title": "A card for construction",
  "quest.2FDE8EE1489DEC78.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Builder & Cards",
  "quest.2FDE8EE1489DEC78.quest_desc": [
    "A normal Shape Card tells the Builder which shape to place. Quarry and void cards are different operations even though they fit the same machine.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Configure a small hollow box, keep the Builder disabled and inspect the support preview. Supply ordinary stone bricks only after the bounds match your test plot.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Read the operation name every time you swap cards. Reusing the same machine does not make the new card behave like the old one."
  ],
  "task.342DDE72BA859EDB.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.37E20C22C48373F0.title": "Give the quarry somewhere to put drops",
  "quest.37E20C22C48373F0.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Builder & Cards",
  "quest.37E20C22C48373F0.quest_desc": [
    "A quarry needs output capacity. Increasing its area without increasing the storage route can leave it stopped on a full adjacent inventory.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Attach a visible output chest and use a tiny selected region away from your base. Run the normal quarry briefly, count recovered blocks, then test that the machine stops/resumes predictably when output fills and clears.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Normal, clearing and void operations have different outcomes. Use a keeping-drops variant for this demonstration."
  ],
  "task.7A96B320312BF936.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.50E3D5C7BFDDD37E.title": "Keep the intermediate inside",
  "quest.50E3D5C7BFDDD37E.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.50E3D5C7BFDDD37E.quest_desc": [
    "A multi-step Crafter should retain the plank intermediate and export the final sticks. This is a practical example of why result handling matters.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Teach logs -> planks and planks -> sticks, reserve their slots and run a small batch. Collect 32 sticks, then inspect leftover planks inside the machine to confirm the intermediate stayed available.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If the second recipe has no ingredients while planks are in the output chest, change the first recipe's result handling."
  ],
  "task.0EA27C4DEDE55116.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.42A58B2D0478330E.title": "Name the arrival point",
  "quest.42A58B2D0478330E.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Travel & Projects",
  "quest.42A58B2D0478330E.quest_desc": [
    "A named receiver is easier to select correctly than several anonymous destinations. Arrival space, power and loading are part of the endpoint.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place the home receiver in a clear room, give it an unmistakable name and verify its energy. Dial it from a nearby transmitter and test arrival before setting up a distant route.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Leave headroom and a walkable exit. A receiver inside a decorative enclosure can be a poor teleport destination even when the network connects."
  ],
  "task.11D8032BF493B05A.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4D97E42D0F6097D0.title": "Display one useful quantity",
  "quest.4D97E42D0F6097D0.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Workshop Utilities",
  "quest.4D97E42D0F6097D0.quest_desc": [
    "A screen becomes useful when a module displays a quantity that changes and tells you something about the workshop.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Configure one supported module, connect its target as the manual describes, and show a stock or energy reading. Change the underlying quantity and verify the display responds.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If the value never changes, verify the target/module configuration before increasing the controller range or screen size."
  ]
}
